y from  SolarWinds Mars although it may have  started off in a similar place is  certainly very different much drier it's  lost nearly all of its atmosphere 99% of  it has gone there's very little water if  life did ever establish itself early on  it's been a very difficult place for it  to hang on NASA's missions have strongly  suggested Mars could have supported life  in a warmer wetter past in 2022 Rovers  will go to Mars  searching for evidence of microbes that  should finally give us the answer Thomas  More Sky News
 

